{"id": "EUVD-2026-103574", "enisaUuid": "1e321cb1-e9e5-3398-b9fe-96af2a5f5fc6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: arizona: Fix runtime PM leak in arizona_gpio_direction_out()\n\nSwitching a persistent GPIO line from input to output acquires a\nruntime PM reference on the parent device, but if the subsequent\nregmap_update_bits() fails the reference is never dropped and no later\ndirection_in() can balance it since the direction was never changed.\nDrop the reference on the update failure path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40c010c1866382cb63ba7497d6ec74fcc60ab9cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61ed58b745c1186006b8357da651abbb7a6bff17", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c8e87f33b68557a725e72f34051299f55c6fa9e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d8d6cddcb7c0b8125f3a9e52492e929674009d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ee200f484983b0a178c593e57d2fe3e67061ee8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9f738487c11fb512dadef097b56020239c21810", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39748357db26b20a02ea2a25ce48943e6c6d6286", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9d810279f84b30738f7790c0ed15f8dd5b9024a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98529", "GHSA-42qh-8w7w-426q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04806da1-af7d-3e97-a999-916683dfb3af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "36e330dd-0af2-3c15-af2e-1a0e7927060e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "3925b0e1-7729-3394-a534-3dd1dfbf4d04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27a49ed17e2245cacbdea88ad78b8494653e0338 <40c010c1866382cb63ba7497d6ec74fcc60ab9cf"}, {"id": "403209aa-7840-3e96-933e-5d6962d11c30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "prod